melody:
# Chorus as published in 1926
Pack up all my care and woe,
B4 B4 B4 B4 C5 B4 B4 r
here I go, sing-ing low,
B4 A4 A4 r A4 G4 G4 r
bye, bye, black-bird.
G4(4) A4(4) G4(2) F#4(2) ~F#4(4)
Where some-bod-y waits for me,
C5 C5 C5 C5 D5 C5 C5 r
sug-ar's sweet, so is she,
C5 B4 B4 r B4 A4 A4 r
bye, bye, black-bird.
A4(4) B4(4) A4(2) G4(2) ~G4(4)
No one here can love and un-der-stand me,
G4 D5 D5 D5 D5 C5 B4 A4 A4(4) G#4(4)
oh, what hard luck stor-ies they all hand me.
E4 C5 C5 C5 C5 B4 A4 G4 G4(4) F#4(4)
Make my bed and light the light,
B4 B4 B4 B4 C5 B4 B4 r
I'll ar-rive late to-night,
B4 A4 A4 r A4 G#4 A4(2)
black-bird, bye, bye.
A4(2) C5(2) ~C5 r F#4(2) G4(2) r(2) r(4)

